		{"id":"62ae64a19cd73bbe","type":"text","text":"\n## **11:35** - Right word, wrong task\n## **11:45** -\tT.A.S.K \n## **11:55** - *C Reading **17, 18a–18d, 19–21**.*\n\n## **12:15** -\tWrap-up and homework reminder","x":-1692,"y":-430,"width":649,"height":212,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"8650ba69df5f6209","type":"text","text":"***Homework***\n- Finish any incomplete **C Reading** **17, 18a–18d, 19–21**..\n","x":-1692,"y":-195,"width":449,"height":131,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"b9ecedb9e62d636c","type":"text","text":"# **Today's Class: Reading And T.A.S.K","x":-1712,"y":-506,"width":828,"height":60,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"efaa703f7c93049c","type":"text","text":"","x":-2169,"y":620,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"deaab107bcd4f182","x":-1692,"y":23,"width":884,"height":734,"color":"6","type":"text","text":"## 1. Before reading\n\n| Strategy                       | What to do                                                                     |\n| ------------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| 1. Predicting                  | Look at the title, pictures and headings. Predict what the text will be about. |\n| 2. Activating prior knowledge  | Think about what you already know about the topic.                             |\n| 3. Skimming                    | Read quickly to understand the general topic and main idea.                    |\n| 4. Reading the questions first | Identify what information you need to find in the text.                        |\n## 2. While reading\n\n|Strategy|What to do|\n|---|---|\n|5. Scanning|Look for specific information, such as names, dates, numbers or keywords.|\n|6. Finding the main idea|Identify the most important message of a paragraph or text.|\n|7. Finding supporting details|Look for examples, explanations and facts that support the main idea.|\n|8. Guessing meaning from context|Use surrounding words and sentences to understand unfamiliar vocabulary.|\n|9. Recognising signal words|Notice words such as because, however, although, first and finally.|\n|10. Recognising false friends|Be careful with English words that look like Dutch words but have different meanings, such as actual and eventually.|\n|11. Making inferences|Combine clues from the text to understand information that is not directly stated.|\n|12. Summarising|Explain the most important information in your own words.|"},
		{"id":"fbf1b2779f1c07ef","x":-496,"y":-506,"width":735,"height":198,"color":"3","type":"text","text":"**Before I answer a question:**\n\n- **T | Task word:** Circle what I must do: *translate, choose, complete, correct, write*.\n- **A | Answer form:** Box the language or form: *English, Dutch, one word, a choice, a sentence*.\n- **S | Special conditions:** Underline anything extra: *TWO, NOT, past simple, only*.\n- **K | Keep checking:** Reread the question. Does my answer do **exactly** what it asks?"}
	],
	"edges":[]
}